      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Larry Johnson (born in Albuquerque, New Mexico) is an American author and former employee of the Alcor Life Extension Foundation (Alcor), a cryonics company for whom he once served as chief operating officer. He received notoriety with the release of the August 13, 2003 issue of \"Sports Illustrated\". \"Sports Illustrated\" sportswriter Tom Verducci, along with Johnson's input, published an article about “What Really Happened to Ted Williams?\" Immediately following the \"Sports Illustrated\" article, Johnson agreed to an interview with Diane Sawyer of Good Morning America.",
